Specialization specialist owns `SPECIALIZATIONS` and spec helpers in `skills.ts` (`sheetPerk`, `choicePerk`, `weaponTypePerks`, `exclusivePerkGroups`, `sanitizeSpecPerks`, `setSpecPerkFlags`, `activeSpecPerks`). Do not edit the `SKILLS` array or `skill-mods.ts`.

Sheet perks default ON. Exclusive tree forks default OFF (player picks one or neither). Weapon-type +5% nodes default OFF.

Do not regress:

- Technician exclusive fork: Overclocked CPU +10% Skill Damage vs Enhanced Diagnostics +10% Skill Repair (`technician-skill-focus`).
- Sharpshooter 15% HSD + 10% MMR; filter the generated weapon-type MMR +5% so it does not double.
- Demolitionist 15% Explosive + 10% LMG; filter the generated weapon-type LMG +5%.
- Gunner 10% Armor on Kill / 25% ammo. Survivalist 10% Incoming Repairs / 10% Status. Firewall 10% Total Armor / 10% Status.
- Keep existing perk `id` slugs.

Combat-only nodes (signature ammo, extra armor kits, skill unlocks, Banshee) stay in the spec `description`. Do not invent Weapon Damage. PvE only — ignore Conflict / PvP DZ tables.

`npm test` after edits. Append-only tests in `src/lib/calc.test.ts`.
